        "original_id": "76a824db-391e-5539-8556-7454bc334cbc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Raymond Jr.\n- Organizations: Mississippi Freedom Democratic Party, Congress of Racial Equality\n- Places: Mississippi\n- Concepts: Civil Rights Movement, Freedom Rides\n\nFacts:\n- George Raymond Jr. was born on January 1, 1943, and died on March 8, 1973.\n- In the 1960s, George Raymond Jr. was an African-American civil rights activist, a Freedom Rider, and the head of the Congress of Racial Equality in Mississippi.\n- George Raymond Jr. was a member of the Mississippi Freedom Democratic Party.\n- The Mississippi Freedom Democratic Party was created in 1964 in Mississippi as an American political party.\n- The Mississippi Freedom Democratic Party was a branch of the populist Freedom Democratic organization during the Civil Rights Movement.",
